DTS core only (owner's decision, 2026-11-12; see docs/RESEARCH.md section 3.2, point 6).

The `dca` decoder keeps only the original DTS core (DTS Coherent Acoustics, up to 5.1 channels):
- the DTS-HD lossless (XLL) and DTS Express (LBR) decoders are not compiled (dca_xll.o, dca_lbr.o leave the
  decoder's object list) and their DSP routines are removed from dcadsp.c;
- the decoder no longer parses the extension sub-stream (DTS-HD, DTS Express, DTS:X) and always decodes the
  core alone (the `core_only` option is gone: it is always on);
- the parsers of the core's own extensions (XCh, XXCH, X96) and of the DTS-HD extensions in the extension
  sub-stream (XBR, X96, XXCH) are removed from dca_core.c.
A DTS-HD or DTS:X stream that carries a backward compatible core plays that core; DTS Express has no core
and does not play. Shared filtering code that would apply an extension stays in dca_core.c and is unreachable. The parser (dca_parser.c)
and the encoder are unchanged.

Applies with `patch -p1` to the pinned FFmpeg archive (third_party/sources.lock); scripts/fetch-sources.sh
applies it.

